{
    "background_story": "Kaizen was a skilled but troubled artist, known for his mesmerizing paintings that seemed to capture the essence of the human condition. However, behind the scenes, Kaizen struggled with a pattern of malingering, often feigning illnesses or injuries to avoid deadlines and commitments. His galleries and patrons would receive frantic calls, claiming he was bedridden with a mysterious ailment, only to see him posting vibrant updates on social media. As his reputation grew, so did the frequency of his 'ailments'. Kaizen's friends and family tried to stage interventions, but he would charm his way out of trouble, always promising to deliver his next masterpiece. The art world was torn between admiration for his talent and frustration with his antics, leaving many to wonder if Kaizen's greatest work of art was the illusion of his own suffering.",
